IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa14-types`

-- Pensions Act 2014 (UK) — GOAL 2: DEFERRAL (s 17).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2014-19.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — deferral`

-- s 17(3) "A person is entitled to one increment for each whole week in the
-- period during which the person's entitlement to a state pension was
-- deferred." The period runs from its first to its last day, both counted.
@ref s 17(3)
@export The number of increments under s 17(3) of the Pensions Act 2014 (UK): one for each whole week in the deferral period, counting its first and last days. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Deferral facts`  @desc The first and last days of the deferral
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the whole weeks deferred in` f MEANS
    IF   days LESS THAN 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR (days DIVIDED BY 7)
    WHERE
        days MEANS Day (f's `deferred until`) MINUS Day (f's `deferred from`) PLUS 1

-- s 17(1) "the weekly rate of the person's state pension is increased by an
-- amount equal to the sum of the increments". (2) "But the weekly rate is not
-- to be increased ... if the increase would be less than 1% of the person's
-- weekly rate ignoring that subsection." (4): each increment is the
-- specified percentage of the weekly rate.
@ref s 17(1)-(4)
@export The weekly increase for deferring a state pension under s 17 of the Pensions Act 2014 (UK): the number of whole weeks deferred times the specified percentage of the weekly rate; nothing if that is less than 1% of the weekly rate. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Deferral facts`  @desc The deferral dates, the weekly rate, and the increment percentage specified in regulations
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly increase for deferral in` f MEANS
    IF   increase LESS THAN f's `weekly rate` TIMES 0.01
    THEN 0
    ELSE increase
    WHERE
        increase MEANS `the whole weeks deferred in` f TIMES f's `increment percentage` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES f's `weekly rate`
